          "visual_type": "text",
          "on_screen_text": "Atom = one basic unit",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.key_takeaways[0]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scene_2",
      "purpose": "Define a molecule as atoms chemically bonded together.",
      "pedagogy_beat_ids": [
        "pedagogy_plan.learning_objectives[1]",
        "pedagogy_plan.teaching_sequence[0]"
      ],
      "estimated_duration_seconds": 45.0,
      "narration_segments": [
        {
          "id": "narr_2_1",
          "text": "Now imagine atoms forming chemical bonds with each other.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_2_2",
          "text": "When atoms bond together, they can make a molecule.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_2_3",
          "text": "A molecule is a group of two or more atoms chemically bonded together.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[1]",
            "verified_chemistry.learning_objectives[0]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_2_4",
          "text": "That means a molecule is not just one atom by itself.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[1]",
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[4]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_2_5",
          "text": "It is made from two or more bonded atoms acting as a distinct unit.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.assumptions[1]",
            "verified_chemistry.key_takeaways[1]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visual_beats": [
        {
          "id": "vis_2_1",
          "trigger_narration_id": "narr_2_1",
          "trigger_phrase": "chemical bonds",
          "action": "Show two separate atoms moving close together; highlight the space where a bond will appear.",
          "visual_type": "molecule_diagram",
          "on_screen_text": "Atoms can bond",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_2_2",
          "trigger_narration_id": "narr_2_2",
          "trigger_phrase": "make a molecule",
          "action": "Draw a bond between the two atoms and group them with a soft outline.",
          "visual_type": "molecule_diagram",
          "on_screen_text": "Bonded atoms form a molecule",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_2_3",
          "trigger_narration_id": "narr_2_3",
          "trigger_phrase": "two or more atoms",
          "action": "Show a molecule diagram with two bonded atoms, then add a small label pointing to each atom and the bond.",
          "visual_type": "molecule_diagram",
          "on_screen_text": "Molecule: 2 or more bonded atoms",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_2_4",
          "trigger_narration_id": "narr_2_4",
          "trigger_phrase": "not just one atom",
          "action": "Place a single atom on the left and a bonded pair on the right; mark the pair as the molecule.",
          "visual_type": "comparison_table",
          "on_screen_text": "One atom ≠ molecule",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[1]",
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[4]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "vis_2_5",
          "trigger_narration_id": "narr_2_5",
          "trigger_phrase": "distinct unit",
          "action": "Keep the bonded atoms grouped with one outline, emphasizing the molecule as one separate unit.",
          "visual_type": "molecule_diagram",
          "on_screen_text": "A bonded distinct unit",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.assumptions[1]"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scene_3",
      "purpose": "Use oxygen and water examples to distinguish same-element and different-element molecules.",
      "pedagogy_beat_ids": [
        "pedagogy_plan.learning_objectives[2]",
        "pedagogy_plan.teaching_sequence[0]"
      ],
      "estimated_duration_seconds": 62.0,
      "narration_segments": [
        {
          "id": "narr_3_1",
          "text": "Let’s test the definition with oxygen gas.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[2]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_2",
          "text": "If two oxygen atoms bond together, they form an oxygen molecule, O2.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.molecules[0]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_3",
          "text": "This molecule contains atoms of the same element, oxygen.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.common_misconceptions[0]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_4",
          "text": "So not every molecule is a compound.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.common_misconceptions[0]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_5",
          "text": "Now compare that with water.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[3]",
            "verified_chemistry.molecules[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_6",
          "text": "If two hydrogen atoms bond with one oxygen atom, they form a water molecule, H2O.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[3]",
            "verified_chemistry.molecules[1]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_7",
          "text": "Water has atoms of different elements, hydrogen and oxygen.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.reasoning_steps[3]"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "narr_3_8",
          "text": "So molecules may be made of the same kind of atom or different kinds of atoms.",
          "source_ids": [
            "verified_chemistry.key_takeaways[2]",
            "verified_chemistry.concepts[2]"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "visual_beats": [
